{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed as Gerrit change 1734 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1), merged to gerrit/main as cecc72b27f.\n\nAGENTS.md now states the rule — an intermittently failing test is a bug to root-cause via /rebar-debug, fix the class not the run, with the three-part rationale in one sentence — and reserves recheck for provably environmental faults with the reasoning stated in the comment. CONTRIBUTING.md section 6 stays the CI-triage home and splits the two cases to opposite remedies instead of contradicting it. The two cross-link.\n\nThe test pins both halves; the second is the load-bearing one, asserting the old retry-until-green licence is ABSENT from both files. Verified by restoring the AGENTS.md sentence and watching it fail.\n\nNote on how this ticket was landed: it was originally stacked on 1731, which is parked behind a macOS xdist worker-crash flake (bug 0078-fa3e). Rather than submit the stack top and drag an ungated ancestor onto main, the stack was re-parented so this change sits directly on main. That ordering discipline is the same concern as the WIP rule in e30d-b5e7-f4de-4f91.\n\nThe rule was also exercised on itself during this batch: change 1731 took two Verified -1s from the same crashed worker on the same macOS cell. It was triaged, filed as a bug with evidence, and NOT rechecked a third time."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786652450265852001,"uuid":"aa092775-60b8-4435-856f-101c88533579"}